{"name":"Cruise","hex":"#b4e2d5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cruise","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Anglo-Norman."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cruise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cruise ship","blocks":[{"text":"Cruise ships are large passenger ships used mainly for vacationing. Unlike ocean liners, which are used for transport, cruise ships typically embark on round-trip voyages to various ports of call, where passengers may go on shore excursions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Icon_of_the_Seas_Puerto_Rico_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Icon_of_the_Seas_Puerto_Rico_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cruise_ship"},{"title":"Booze cruise","blocks":[{"text":"In British slang, a booze cruise is a brief trip from Britain to France or Belgium with the intent of taking advantage of lower prices, and buying personal supplies of (especially) alcohol or tobacco in bulk quantities. This is a legally allowed process not to be confused with smuggling."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Normandy_%2710-_Booze_Cruise_%40_Englesqueville_La_Percee_%284824879876%29.jpg/330px-Normandy_%2710-_Booze_Cruise_%40_Englesqueville_La_Percee_%284824879876%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booze_cruise"},{"title":"Cruise (autonomous vehicle)","blocks":[{"text":"Cruise LLC was an American self-driving car company that became a subsidiary of General Motors, headquartered in San Francisco, California. Founded in 2013 by Kyle Vogt and Dan Kan, Cruise tested and developed autonomous car technology. The company was acquired by General Motors in 2016, and operated as a largely autonomous subsidiary, focusing on producing a fleet of driverless taxis. Following a series of incidents, 